Error [E2402]: `?` can't convert `[FieldError]` into `Err` — no declared conversion exists
  --> tests/ui/env_config_decode_error.jet:11:19
    |
 11 |     failed :: env.decode<Settings>(prefix: "APP_", file: "", allow: ["APP_PORT"])
    |                   ^^^^^^
 Why: `?` uses the declared conversion rail; `[FieldError]` can reach `Err` only through `impl [FieldError] -> Err`
 Fix: add `impl [FieldError] -> Err { … }` before this function, or change the return type
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E2402

Error [E0107]: nothing named `errors` exists here
  --> tests/ui/env_config_decode_error.jet:14:43
    |
 14 |         .Err(errors) -> { panic("config: {errors}") }
    |                                           ^^^^^^
 Why: a name must be declared before it's used
 Fix: declare it first: `errors :: ...`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0107

Error [E0003]: this `if` needs an `else` arm
  --> tests/ui/env_config_decode_error.jet:12:5
    |
 12 |     if failed == {
    |     ^^
 Why: mixed condition arms (or non-pattern arms) must always have a fallback (D-IF1)
 Fix: add `else -> { ... }` after the last arm
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0003
